#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmouth; is a program that enables persons that cannot speak to let their "
"computers speak. It includes a history of spoken sentences from which the "
"user can select sentences to be re-spoken."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that &kmouth; does not include speech synthesizer. Instead it requires "
"a speech synthesizer installed in the system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid "Please report any problems and feature requests to the author of &kmouth;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kmouth;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "The first start"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"During the first start of &kmouth;, a wizard is displayed into which you can "
"enter some basic configuration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The wizard</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The wizard</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With the first page of the wizard (the left screen shot) you specify the "
"command that shall later be used for the text-to-speech conversion. For more "
"details look into the <link linkend=\"tts-config\">description of the "
"configuration dialog.</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With the second page you select which standard phrase books you need. From "
"the phrase books you later can select often used phrases so that you do not "
"need to type them in. Of course &kmouth; also has an edit dialog for the "
"case that you later want to edit your phrase books."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With the third page (the right screen shot) you define the dictionary for a "
"word completion. &kmouth; will parse the &kde; documentation of the chosen "
"language in order to detect the frequentness of individual words. Optionally "
"you can compare the word list to an OpenOffice.org dictionary in order to "
"only add correctly spelled words to the word completion."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Main Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main window of &kmouth; is fairly simple. It consists basically of an "
"edit field into which you type your sentences (the lower white field in the "
"screen shot) and a history of spoken sentences (the upper white field in the "
"screen shot)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid "The main window of &kmouth;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:134 index.docbook:175 index.docbook:244 index.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screen shot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Assuming that you have correctly <link linkend=\"config-dialog\">configured "
"&kmouth;</link> you can use the edit field for entering sentences you want "
"to hear. Once a sentence got spoken it will be appended to the history. From "
"the history you can select sentences to be re-spoken."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"From the phrase books (located in the line below the tool bar) you can "
"select often used phrases."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Configuration Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By using the menu entry <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &kmouth;...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> you "
"open the configuration dialog of &kmouth;. This dialog consists of the pages "
"<guilabel>General Options</guilabel> with the two tabs <guilabel>Text-to-"
"Speech</guilabel> and <guilabel>Preferences</guilabel>, the page "
"<guilabel>Word Completion</guilabel> and the page <guilabel>KTTSD Speech "
"Service</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Text-to-Speech</guilabel> tab</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Text-to-Speech</guilabel> tab</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Into the edit field of the <guilabel>Text-to-Speech</guilabel> tab you enter "
"the command for calling the speech synthesizer. With the combo box below the "
"edit field you specify the character encoding that is used for passing the "
"text to the speech synthesizer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmouth; knows two ways of passing the text: If the command expects the text "
"as standard input you select the check box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The other way is to pass the text as a parameter: Before calling the command "
"&kmouth; replaces certain placeholders with actual content:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid "Placeholder"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replaced with"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: token
#: index.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid "<token>%t</token>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid "The actual text that should be spoken"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: token
#: index.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid "<token>%f</token>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "The name of a temporary file that contains the text that should be spoken"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: token
#: index.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid "<token>%l</token>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid "The language code associated with the current word completion dictionary"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: token
#: index.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid "<token>%%</token>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid "A percent sign"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Off course the command for speaking texts is dependent on which speech "
"synthesizer you use. Please look into the documentation of your speech "
"synthesizer for the command for speaking texts. You can find examples for "
"the command in the <link linkend=\"tts\">appendix</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <guilabel>Use KTTSD speech service if possible</guilabel> you "
"tell &kmouth; first to try to send the text to the KTTSD speech service. If "
"this succeeds the other configuration entries on this tab are ignored. The "
"KTTSD speech service is a &kde; daemon which gives &kde; applications a "
"standardized interface for speech synthesis and is currently developed in "
"<acronym>SVN</acronym>. It is safe to select this option even if KTTSD is "
"not installed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Preferences</guilabel> tab</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Preferences</guilabel> tab</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Preferences</guilabel> tab contains options that alter the "
"behavior of &kmouth; in certain situations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With the first combo box, <guilabel>Selection of phrases in the phrase book:"
"</guilabel>, you specify which action is triggered by typing the shortcut of "
"a phrase or by selecting a phrase in the <guimenu>Phrase Book</guimenu> menu "
"or in the phrase book bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <guilabel>Speak Immediately</guilabel> the selected phrase gets "
"immediately spoken and is entered into the history. If you select "
"<guilabel>Insert Into Edit Field</guilabel> the selected phrase is just "
"inserted into the edit field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With the second combo box, <guilabel>Closing the phrase book edit window:</"
"guilabel>, you specify whether the phrase book gets saved if you just close "
"the phrase book edit window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:271
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <guilabel>Save Phrase Book</guilabel> the phrase book gets "
"saved. If you select <guilabel>Discard changes</guilabel> the changes are "
"discarded and the phrase book is not saved. If you select <guilabel>Ask "
"Whether to Save</guilabel> &kmouth; will ask you whether it shall save the "
"phrase book."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The <guilabel>Word Completion</guilabel> page</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Word Completion</guilabel> page</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:298
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Word Completion</guilabel> page contains a list of "
"dictionaries used for the word completion. (&kmouth; will display a combo "
"box next to the edit field in the main window if this list contains more "
"than one dictionary. You can use this combo box in order to select the "
"dictionary that actually gets used for the word completion.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With the buttons on the right side of the page you can add and delete "
"dictionaries, change the order of the dictionaries or export dictionaries to "
"a file. With the edit field and the combo box below the list you can change "
"the name and the language associated with the dictionary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid "When you add a new dictionary you may choose between several sources:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create a new dictionary from the &kde; documentation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:319
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you use this source &kmouth; will ask you for the intended language and "
"afterwards parse the &kde; documentation. The frequentness of the individual "
"words is detect by simply counting the occurrences of each word. Optionally "
"you can compare the word list to an OpenOffice.org dictionary in order to "
"only add correctly spelled words to the new dictionary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create a new dictionary from a file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you use this source &kmouth; will ask you for the intended file. You may "
"either select an &XML; file, a standard text file or a file containing a "
"word completion dictionary created by either &kmouth; or GOK (the GNOME On-"
"screen Keyboard). If you select a standard text file or an &XML; file the "
"frequentness of the individual words is detected by simply counting the "
"occurrences of each word. Optionally you can compare the word list to an "
"OpenOffice.org dictionary in order to only add correctly spelled words to "
"the new dictionary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create a new dictionary from a folder"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you use this source &kmouth; will ask you for the intended folder. "
"&kmouth; will open all files in that folder and its subdirectories. Each "
"file is either loaded as a completion dictionary, as an &XML; file or as a "
"standard text file. In the latter two cases the occurrences of each "
"individual word in the file is counted. Optionally you can compare the word "
"list to an OpenOffice.org dictionary in order to only add correctly spelled "
"words to the new dictionary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid "Merge dictionaries"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use this option in order to merge the available dictionaries. "
"&kmouth; will ask you which dictionaries should be merged and how the "
"individual dictionaries should be weighted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create an empty word list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use this option in order to create a blank dictionary without any "
"entries. As &kmouth; automatically adds newly typed words to the "
"dictionaries it will learn your vocabulary with the time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>KTTSD Speech Service</guilabel> page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The configuration of the &kde; Speech Service is described in detail in the "
"<ulink url=\"help:kttsd\">KTTS Handbook</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Phrase Book Edit Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By using the menu entry <menuchoice> <guimenu>Phrase Books</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Edit...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> you open the phrase "
"book edit window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:389
#, no-c-format
msgid "The phrase book edit window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screens hot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:403
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main area of the phrase book edit window is divided into two parts. "
"Within the upper part the phrase books are displayed in some tree structure."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Within the lower part you may modify a selected item. If you have selected a "
"phrase you can modify the contents of the phrase as well as its shortcut. If "
"you have selected a phrase book you can only change its name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:414
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Actions like adding new phrases and phrase books and deleting selected "
"phrases and phrase books can be done by selecting them in either the menu "
"bar, the toolbar or a pop up menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:419
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can change the order of the phrase books and phrases by dragging them to "
"their new places or by using the arrow keys while the &Alt; key is pressed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:429
#, no-c-format
msgid "Command Reference"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid "Commands Within The Main Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:434 index.docbook:707
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>File</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>O</keycap></keycombo> </shortcut> "
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Open as History...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:444 index.docbook:687
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opens a text file into as history of spoken sentences."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:447
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>S</keycap></keycombo> </shortcut> "
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Save History As...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:454 index.docbook:696
#, no-c-format
msgid "Saves the history into a text file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:457
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>P</keycap></keycombo> </shortcut> "
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Print History...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:464
#, no-c-format
msgid "Prints the history."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:467
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>Q</keycap></keycombo> </shortcut> "
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Quit</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:474
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quits &kmouth;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:480 index.docbook:778
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:483 index.docbook:781
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>X</keycap></keycombo> </shortcut> "
"<guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Cut</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Cuts the selected section and puts it to the clipboard. If there is some "
"text selected in the edit field it is placed it on the clipboard. Otherwise "
"the selected sentences in the history (if any) are placed on the clipboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:498 index.docbook:793
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>C</keycap></keycombo> </shortcut> "
"<guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Copy</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:505
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Copies the selected section to the clipboard. If there is some text selected "
"in the edit field it is copied to the clipboard. Otherwise the selected "
"sentences in the history (if any) are copied to the clipboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:513 index.docbook:805
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>V</keycap></keycombo> </shortcut> "
"<guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Paste</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:520
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Pastes the clipboard contents at the current cursor position into the edit "
"field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:526
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Speak</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:530
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Speaks the currently active sentence(s). If there is some text in the edit "
"field it is spoken. Otherwise the selected sentences in the history (if any) "
"are spoken."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:540
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Phrase Books</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:543
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Phrase Books</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Edit...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:547
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opens the <link linkend=\"phrasebook-editor\">phrase book edit window</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:555
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:558
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>M</keycap></keycombo> </shortcut> "
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Menubar</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:565
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked, this displays the menubar. When unchecked the menubar is "
"hidden."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:571
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Toolbar</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:575
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action> When checked, this displays a movable toolbar containing buttons "
"used to initiate frequently used commands. The toolbar is most commonly "
"located at the top of the editor just under the menu. When unchecked the "
"toolbar is hidden. </action> Clicking on the striated grip and dragging "
"allows the user to move the bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:587
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Statusbar</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:591
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked, this displays a small bar at the bottom of the main window "
"containing information about the status of &kmouth;. When unchecked the "
"status bar is hidden."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:598
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Phrasebook Bar</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:602
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action> When checked, this displays a movable phrasebook bar containing "
"buttons for the phrasebook entries. The phrasebook bar is most commonly "
"located at the top of the editor just under the toolbar. When unchecked the "
"phrasebook bar is hidden. </action> Clicking on the striated grip and "
"dragging allows the user to move the bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:614
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure KMouth...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:618
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Opens the <link linkend=\"config-dialog\">configuration dialog for the "
"speech synthesizer</link> and other &kmouth; settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:627 index.docbook:829
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Help</guimenu> Menu"
